{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-s4-s3-half-symmetric-projection","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:s4-s3-half-symmetric-projection","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of s4 s3 half symmetric projection","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-s4-s3-half-symmetric-projection"],"text":"s4-s3-half-symmetric-projection-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:s4-s3-half-symmetric-projection\"></a><p>By the standard <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S_n</code> branching rule (remove one box from\nthe Young diagram of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda \\vdash 4</code> to obtain the restriction\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda \\downarrow S_3</code>):</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda \\vdash 4</code></th>\n<th align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\dim V_\\lambda</code></th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda \\downarrow S_3</code></th>\n<th align=\"right\">Trivial <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(3)</code> content</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(4)</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\">1</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(3)</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\">1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(3,1)</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\">3</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(3) + (2,1)</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\">1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(2,2)</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\">2</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(2,1)</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(2,1,1)</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\">3</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(2,1) + (1^3)</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1^4)</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\">1</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1^3)</code></td>\n<td align=\"right\">0</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The half-symmetric part takes one representative of each conjugate pair\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{(4), (1^4)\\}</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{(3,1), (2,1,1)\\}</code>, with weight <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>, and the\nself-conjugate <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(2,2)</code> with weight <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tfrac{1}{2}</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\dim_{\\text{half-sym}} = 1 + 3 + \\tfrac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 = 5, \\qquad\n  \\text{trivial } S_3 \\text{ content} = 1 + 1 + \\tfrac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 = 2.</code></pre>\n<p>Hence the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S_3</code>-trivial share is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2/5</code>. <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\square</code></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/s4-s3-half-symmetric-projection-proof.md","heading":"Proof","page":"b/prf-s4-s3-half-symmetric-projection","qa":{"counts":{"pass":55,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":71}}}
